    "body": "## Security impact\n\n`GET /jobs/{id}` is publicly reachable, while `JobVisibilityService` previously returned immediately for anonymous callers. Because the endpoint accepted any numeric ID, jobs that had already left public discovery (`IN_PROGRESS`, `DONE`, `CANCELLED`, etc.) could still be enumerated directly and their detail DTOs exposed to unauthenticated or unrelated callers.\n\n## Fix\n\n- load the job before granting anonymous access;\n- keep public detail access restricted to `OPEN` jobs;\n- preserve access for the job owner and assigned worker after lifecycle transitions;\n- return the existing neutral `ResourceNotFoundException` for outsiders on non-public lifecycle states;\n- preserve user-block filtering for open jobs.\n\n## Regression coverage\n\nAdds tests proving that:\n- anonymous users can still view `OPEN` jobs;\n- anonymous users cannot enumerate `IN_PROGRESS` jobs;\n- authenticated outsiders cannot enumerate `DONE` jobs;\n- owner/worker retain access after completion;\n- existing blocked/unblocked open-job behavior remains intact.\n\n## CI follow-up\n\nThe first exact-head run exposed a test-only compile error where the regression used the non-existent enum value `COMPLETED`; the domain's canonical completed status is `DONE`. Commit `2766bd51ce23f4aa2a41735bd2eec82b9e518f4a` corrects the test and the full exact-head gate is rerunning.",
